<div data-cgap-sector="Marine, Ports &amp; Shipyards" data-cgap-term="marina"></div><p class="lead">Electric Shock Drowning is the most ordered sign in our whole catalog, and for good reason: the danger in the water around a dock cannot be seen, and swimmers rarely know that a faulty boat or pedestal can put current in the water.</p><p>This page collects signs for the rest of the waterfront too: shore power pedestals and cords, fuel docks, boat lifts and travel lifts, launch ramps and boat yards, gangways and piers, mooring gear, and the hot work and confined spaces of a shipyard. They are rust-resistant aluminum made for sun, spray and wet docks.</p><h2>What to post, and where</h2><div class="il-areas"><div class="il-area il-best"><h3>Most ordered</h3><p>The signs customers in this industry order most.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/cgap-safety-danger-electric-shock-drowning-hazard-sign-8x12-in-aluminum-no-swimming-near-docks-safety-sign-for-marinas-lake-homes">Electric Shock Drowning</a></li><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/fuel-storage-area-danger-sign-flammable-liquids-for-fuel-bunkering-operations-8x12-uv-resistant-rust-resistant-aluminum-professional-facility-grade-by-cgap-safety">Fuel Storage Area</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Shore power and electric shock drowning</h3><p>Pedestals, shore cords and the water around them. 108 signs. Typical spot: Mount on the shore power pedestal door beside the plug.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/cgap-safety-danger-electric-shock-drowning-hazard-sign-8x12-in-aluminum-no-swimming-near-docks-safety-sign-for-marinas-lake-homes">Electric Shock Drowning</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-shore-power-plug-sign-cgap-w02220-812">Shore Power Plug</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-pier-end-pedestal-sign-cgap-c07529-812">Pier End Pedestal</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-pedestal-light-sign-cgap-n02209-812">Pedestal Light</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Fuel docks</h3><p>Fueling, spill response and no smoking at the fuel dock. 126 signs. Typical spot: On the pump house door or coupling guard of the marina fuel transfer pump.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/fuel-storage-area-danger-sign-flammable-liquids-for-fuel-bunkering-operations-8x12-uv-resistant-rust-resistant-aluminum-professional-facility-grade-by-cgap-safety">Fuel Storage Area</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-marina-fuel-pump-drive-sign-cgap-w01420-812">Marina Fuel Pump Drive</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-fuel-dock-gate-sign-cgap-c17594-812">Fuel Dock Gate</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-fuel-tank-vent-sign-cgap-n24688-812">Fuel Tank Vent</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Boat lifts and travel lifts</h3><p>Lift controls, load checks and the area under a lifted boat. 169 signs. Typical spot: Boat lift posts and lift control switch.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-boat-lift-cradle-sign-8x12-aluminum">Boat Lift Cradle</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-dry-stack-forklift-sign-cgap-w19079-812">Dry Stack Forklift</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-battery-hoist-sign-cgap-c21448-812">Battery Hoist</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-boat-lift-bunks-sign-cgap-n01740-812">Boat Lift Bunks</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Launch ramps and boat yards</h3><p>Ramps, haul out areas and boats on stands. 49 signs. Typical spot: Boat storage yard rows and blocked hulls.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-boat-stands-sign-8x12-aluminum">Boat Stands</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-launch-ramp-winch-sign-cgap-w19060-812">Launch Ramp Winch</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-battery-cart-ramp-sign-cgap-c21657-812">Battery Cart Ramp</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-slipway-cradle-winch-sign-cgap-n16079-812">Slipway Cradle Winch</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Docks, gangways and piers</h3><p>Dock edges, gangways, ladders and slips. 65 signs. Typical spot: Gangway foot on the quay and head at the ship.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-vessel-gangway-sign-8x12-aluminum">Vessel Gangway</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-port-gangway-hinge-pin-sign-cgap-w09423-812">Port Gangway Hinge Pin</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-dry-dock-gangway-sign-cgap-c10156-812">Dry Dock Gangway</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-dock-cart-lane-sign-cgap-n10559-812">Dock Cart Lane</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Shipyard hot work and confined spaces</h3><p>Tanks, voids, blasting and hot work on vessels. 98 signs. Typical spot: Ballast tank manholes and access hatches.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-ship-ballast-tank-sign-8x12-aluminum">Ship Ballast Tank</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-uv-ballast-sign-cgap-w19077-812">Uv Ballast</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-vessel-ballast-tank-sign-cgap-c12715-812">Vessel Ballast Tank</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-hot-work-in-tank-sign-cgap-n16215-812">Hot Work In Tank</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Mooring, capstans and winches</h3><p>Lines under load, capstans and winches. 175 signs. Typical spot: Capstan housing and foot control.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-wharf-capstan-sign-8x12-aluminum">Wharf Capstan</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-capstan-sign-cgap-w02219-812">Capstan</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-winch-locker-sign-cgap-c15328-812">Winch Locker</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-winch-drum-sign-cgap-n13319-812">Winch Drum</a></li></ul></div><div class="il-area"><h3>Port terminals and cranes</h3><p>Container yards, cranes and cargo handling. 205 signs. Typical spot: Container yard blocks and empty depots where reach stackers work.</p><ul><li><span data-s="DANGER">DANGER</span><a href="/products/danger-reach-stacker-sign-8x12-aluminum">Reach Stacker</a></li><li><span data-s="WARNING">WARNING</span><a href="/products/warning-container-door-sign-cgap-w02224-812">Container Door</a></li><li><span data-s="CAUTION">CAUTION</span><a href="/products/caution-cargo-log-yard-sign-cgap-c19416-812">Cargo Log Yard</a></li><li><span data-s="NOTICE">NOTICE</span><a href="/products/notice-sts-crane-rail-sign-cgap-n18371-812">STS Crane Rail</a></li></ul></div></div><h2>Common questions</h2><div class="il-faq"><details><summary>Where should Electric Shock Drowning signs go?</summary><p>Post them where people could get into the water near docks with shore power: dock entrances, swim ladders, the end of each pier and near the pedestals. Search &quot;electric shock drowning&quot; to see the sign.</p></details><details><summary>Will these signs hold up on a dock?</summary><p>Yes. They are rust-resistant aluminum with UV-stable print and pre-drilled corners for pilings, rails and pedestal posts.</p></details><details><summary>Do you have signs for boat lifts and fuel docks?</summary><p>Yes, including lift controls and load checks, fuel dock attendant and no smoking signs. Search the equipment name to see them.</p></details></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Where should Electric Shock Drowning signs go?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Post them where people could get into the water near docks with shore power: dock entrances, swim ladders, the end of each pier and near the pedestals. Search \"electric shock drowning\" to see the sign."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Will these signs hold up on a dock?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. They are rust-resistant aluminum with UV-stable print and pre-drilled corners for pilings, rails and pedestal posts."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you have signs for boat lifts and fuel docks?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, including lift controls and load checks, fuel dock attendant and no smoking signs. Search the equipment name to see them."}}]}</script>